<title>PERU: Peru's July coffee output falls 0.93 percent.</title>
<headline>Peru's July coffee output falls 0.93 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's July coffee production fell 0.93 percent to 15,498 tonnes, compared with the same month last year, Agriculture Ministry said Tuesday.</p>
<p>Coffee output for the first seven months, however, was up 10.47 percent at 102,029 tonnes against the same 1995 period.</p>
<p>Coffee exports rose 19.4 percent in July to 16,883 tonnes, worth $38.6 million, while exports in the first seven months gained 41 percent to 105,628 tonnes, worth $118.2 million, the ministry said.</p>
<p>Peru, whose principal coffee harvest is between April and November, is South America's number four producer after Brazil, Colombia and Ecuador, according to the government.</p>
<p>--Andrew Cawthorne, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134</p>
</text>
